     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and labeling allows up to 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual 500\u20131,000 mg per administration. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 1,700 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.**\n- Something else.\n\nIf you confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
